WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.100
--Morning!
--Good morning!
--Morning!

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.980
"Class 2-4"

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.560
--It's been a while.
--Happy new year.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.900
You, too.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.940
Shido? Why are you spaced out?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.410
Huh? Oh. There's a lot on my mind.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.540
Spirits were humans in the beginning?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.540
Oh, hold up.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.210
I mean, I know I was,
so I figured the others were, too.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:33.130
Though now that Raziel's incomplete,
I doubt I can look into it again.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.890
I never could find out much
about the Spirit of Origin.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:44.480
Having said that,
my power isn't completely gone.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.900
I think I'll be able to hinder Westcott
from using Future Entry.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.950
Artemisia Ashcroft is
the British Anti-Spirit Team's ace.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.700
As far as Wizards go,
she's way better than me.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:06.420
But I always thought she hated DEM,
so I wonder why she joined Westcott?

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.630
I hope everyone had a wonderful break!

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.800
Today starts our third semester
in a brand new year.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:25.600
My birthday's not till March, though.
How old do you think I am?

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:32.110
Since I refuse to turn "thirty,"
I'm gonna call it "sirty."

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.070
Clever, right?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.660
T-Tammie?

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:43.990
So now when you speak to me,
please refer to me as "Sir."

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.370
S-Sir! Yes, Sir!

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.210
Sir! Did something happen, Sir?

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:55.170
Oh, nothing much. Just my best friend
Eri deciding on her wedding date.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.260
So happy for her...

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:07.390
Yet I'm still unclaimed. It seems
the god of tying the knot hates me.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.150
Okay! Let's take attendance!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.650
"Class 2-4"

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.820
--Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!
--Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.360
Sir! You're not okay, Sir!

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.780
Sir! You need a break, Sir!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.120
Sir! That's so lame, Sir!

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.870
No, no, it's all right!

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:33.790
But if a demon appeared to grant
a wish in exchange for my soul,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:38.550
I might just say:
"Send an asteroid at Japan, please!"

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:43.890
Abracadabra! Drop on asteroid on me!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.270
--An asteroid?!
--Did Tammie summon one?!

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.990
--Tammie!
--Tammie!

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.860
Shido, that's...

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.410
Shido, head to temp command.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.620
Huh? You mean...?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.250
Yeah. It's a Spirit.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.010
The Spirits?

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.180
They're on standby like you asked.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.810
What happened?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.810
Check this out.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.650
Something fell in the schoolyard, right?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:02.360
The same thing happened in
all of these locations simultaneously.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.780
Everywhere, simultaneously?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:10.120
DEM and other country's
Anti-Spirit Teams were hit, too.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.500
It's possible they targeted
Spirit power and magic.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.830
Targeted? Who?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.590
Her?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.720
Yeah. It's a Spirit
we've never seen before.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:29.680
We're giving her the code name, "Zodiac."

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:41.570
This video is from three hours ago.
DEM discovered Zodiac first.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:48.070
We noticed odd movements from
DEM ships and probed the area.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:53.120
Westcott most likely found her
using Beelzebub.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.040
Though incomplete,
he must have managed it somehow.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.220
Segva.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.770
So that's her Angel?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.110
Yes, "Michael."

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:30.740
Jabbing that key into things can lock
and close off their abilities.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.420
Lataib.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.570
An attack?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.610
It's another of Michael's powers.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.570
The key is put into "space"

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:15.660
and opens up something
resembling a warp gate.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.790
She's able to control
where the portals will exit.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.750
I see! So the asteroid at school...!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:28.130
Correct. It's how Zodiac
carried out her attack on Earth.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.880
She opened up gates in space

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.390
and tossed DEM ship debris through.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:41.060
She was probably upset at being
woken from her nice little nap.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.310
What will we do? Go to space?

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.900
Don't worry. I've got an idea.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.410
It's a 3D projection.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.950
If we project it into space
along with a camera,

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.660
you can talk to her
like you're actually there.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.960
Now then, it's time for long-distance love
between Earth and space!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.510
H-Hey. Hi there.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:16.680
Kotori, help! My head! It's blown off!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.850
Relax! It's still attached.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.810
Calm down! I'm not an enemy.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.360
Hold on!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.240
I...!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:37.820
Talk about aggressive!
I've died five times already!

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:41.790
Mm. I didn't think
she would be this violent.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:45.330
It's a good thing
we went with a projection.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.960
Strange. Why aren't you dead yet?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:56.300
Finally, we're talking.
It's 'cuz I'm being projected here.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:01.180
Projected? Hmm... That's strange.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.560
Would you mind telling me your name?

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.650
Mukuro. Mukuro Hoshimiya.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.440
I see. I...

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.820
"1. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be friends."

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.360
"2. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be lovers."

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.860
"3. I'm Shido Itsuka, your future husband.
I'm gonna make your body crave me."

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.860
"1. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be friends."
"2. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be lovers."
"3. I'm Shido Itsuka, your future husband. I'm gonna make your body crave me."

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.870
Your choices, everyone!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.870
"1. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be friends."
"2. I'm Shido Itsuka. Let's be lovers."
"3. I'm Shido Itsuka, your future husband. I'm gonna make your body crave me."

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.500
I see. Three.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.170
Yeah. One and two work,
but let's go on the offensive.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:34.210
We haven't seen her happiness
move either way yet.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:36.340
We need to get a reaction.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.050
Shido, do three.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.300
Three?!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.890
Whatever happens,
it's not like you're gonna die.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:47.600
We wanna see what sort of
reaction it gets. Hurry up.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:54.030
I'm Shido Itsuka, your future husband.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:58.740
I-I'm gonna make your body... crave me.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.030
Shido Itsuka, huh?

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.490
That's it?!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.160
How are her levels looking?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.290
No changes across the board.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:11.630
Levels are so flat, it's scary.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:16.760
What is your goal? Why did you come here?

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:22.300
I go around trying
to help Spirits like you.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.070
Ratatoskr?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:40.160
There are nine others like Muku
whom you've already helped?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:46.370
Yeah. So can you come to the surface
and let me seal your power?

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.370
I refuse.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:54.340
While I understand your objective,
Muku does not need your help.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.340
I'm content floating up here.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:02.220
B-But DEM might come attack you again!

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:08.060
That scrap metal? Come as they may,
they're hardly an enemy.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:14.230
But the surface is lots of fun.
It's sad up here by yourself.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:18.990
It's not an issue. Muku doesn't feel sad.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:21.150
No need to act tough.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.160
It's not like that.
Muku doesn't feel loneliness.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:32.080
Nor sadness, anger, excitement,
delight, joy, nor love.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.420
Muku has locked her heart.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.750
Locked... your heart?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.720
Why do that?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:47.680
I wonder why? It was so long ago,
it's hard to remember.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:53.560
Muku wants for nothing to touch her heart.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.690
That's why Muku's here,
where no one can reach.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.820
That's... But that's so sad!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:07.080
Please! Come down to Earth
so you can be happy!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.410
You don't get to decide
what makes Muku happy.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:15.040
Perhaps there are Spirits you've saved.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.290
But Muku is Muku.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.750
Leave me out of it.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.800
Th-That's...

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:28.050
Supposing you seal my power,
can you guarantee Muku will be safe?

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:35.520
Would not the Spirits you "save"
be exposed to greater peril?

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.520
Shido, I tire hearing of this hypocrisy.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:46.780
If people don't learn to leave
Muku alone, let's see...

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:51.490
I shall use Michael
to stop this planet's spin.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.830
Goodbye, Shido. May we not meet again.

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.080
Segva.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.010
The image was cut!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.380
The camera's not responding!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.270
Ow!

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.890
You're that depressed
over getting shot down?

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.860
I understand her view.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.770
If not for us,

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:25.950
some Spirits might've had
better futures and be better off.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.240
But don't forget:
Spirits cause huge disasters, too.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:35.750
A power that dangerous looming above us
is something we can't ignore.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:39.500
But if we leave her alone,
she won't do anything.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.300
Even if we don't, what about DEM?

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:49.140
If DEM beats Mukuro,
Westcott will gain her power.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:53.640
And if they fail,
Mukuro will devastate the Earth.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:59.940
We have no choice but to seal
Mukuro's powers before DEM gets her.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.230
You're right. I guess we've gotta.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.440
Well? What are they saying?

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.610
Request. Stop pushing me.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.620
Shh! They'll hear!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:16.040
What are you guys doing?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:20.630
Mm. Sorry. We didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:26.970
Don't apologize! In fact, it's only
natural we're worried about Darling!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:32.930
We may have overheard a little.
Is there any way we can help?

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.430
There's just one option:

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:39.980
Use her Angel to open
the very same heart she closed.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.150
In other words,
use Michael on Mukuro again.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:50.030
I see! But we can't do that
without going to her in person.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.990
Don't worry. I've got a plan.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:53.950
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:58.000
What good timing.
There's something I wanna show you.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.340
Fraxinus' bridge?

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:10.130
No, it's different than before.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:16.850
Yup. It's a new model with
everything upgraded: Fraxinus Excelsior!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.810
Space is a cakewalk for her!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:23.650
Hello, Fraxinus. How goes it?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.820
Welcome, Kotori. It's good to see you.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:27.690
Wha--?!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.150
How rude, Shido.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.070
Were I a Spirit,
my happiness would drop.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:38.330
It's Fraxinus' AI. The upgrades
made it able to converse.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:43.920
My call sign is MARIA. It's a pleasure
to work with you again, Shido.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.880
Yeah. It's a pleasure, MARIA.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.670
So? How long till we can depart, MARIA?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.840
Roughly 90 minutes.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:57.430
I've restored everyone's customizations,

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:01.230
but please confirm them individually.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.440
--Roger!
--Roger!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:06.860
Also, please limit personal goods
brought on the bridge.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.610
You do not need straw dolls
or anime figures.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:11.570
You're kidding!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.360
You never complained before!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.530
Because I couldn't speak.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:22.290
Also, please refrain from
calling ex-wives and call girls.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.370
--Eh?!
--Eh?!

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:27.420
Cameras are not to be used
to spy on past lovers.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.000
No way!

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:33.220
You guys were using
Fraxinus for such things?

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.010
--No!
--As if!
--We'd never!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:40.520
Kotori, an on-base visitor
is asking for a meeting.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.560
Meeting?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.890
It's Chairman Elliot Woodman.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.140
The chairman?!

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:47.020
You know him, Shido?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:50.070
No, the name rings no bells.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.990
Hey. It's been a while.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.370
You're...!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:05.540
I remember! You asked for directions.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.790
That I did.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.130
Allow me to reintroduce myself:

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.720
I'm Elliot Baldwin Woodman.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.550
Kotori? Who is he?

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:24.140
He's the chairman of Ratatoskr's
decision-making round table.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.640
He's it's head and founder.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:35.360
Shido Itsuka, you have my thanks.
Thank you for saving so many Spirits.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:41.030
Uh, no, thank you.
Without Ratatoskr, I'd get nowhere.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:46.370
I've got questions.
First off, Elliot Baldwin Woodman...

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.250
That is you, right?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.130
Yes.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:54.090
Tell me: As one of DEM's
founding members,

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:58.470
what's your goal behind saving
Spirits, when 30 years ago,

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:01.720
it was you who first manifested them?

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.560
They manifested... Spirits?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.270
If you hadn't manifested
Spirits and made DEM,

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:13.570
we wouldn't have had
to go through all this.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.320
What exactly are you plotting?

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:22.740
I see. You have the power
to look up anything, don't you?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.620
You must have done so to me long ago.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.250
I never meant to hide anything.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:36.210
Yes, I founded DEM along with
Isaac Westcott and Ellen Mathers

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:40.050
hoping to utilize the power of Spirits.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:46.470
But laying eyes upon the Spirit of Origin
changed me forever.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:50.770
I left DEM with Karen Mathers here,

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:54.270
who felt the same as me.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.610
Mathers...

00:18:55.610 --> 00:19:02.320
She is Ellen Mathers' little sister,
though Ellen looks like the younger one.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:09.500
Anyway, I dedicated my life
to the protection of Spirits,

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.880
despite making enemies of Ike and Ellen.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.300
What exactly happened?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.800
Love. Love happened.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:21.800
Love?

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:28.640
The moment I saw the Spirit of Origin,
she stole my heart away.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:39.360
That's why I can't stand seeing
other Spirits like her in pain--

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.860
as silly a reason as it seems.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.870
I don't think it's silly.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:52.420
Actually, I'm kinda glad Ratatoskr
was founded by someone like you.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:59.420
Thank you. Sorry, but can I get
a better look at your face?

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.470
Huh? Um, sure.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:11.180
I see. You look like the boy after all...

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.230
Huh?

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:21.150
Emergency! Confirming DEM airship above!
We're under attack!

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.490
You're kidding! How did they find us?

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:26.990
Beelzebub!

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.220
Commander Itsuka, take the Fraxinus.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:50.970
Once I deal with things here,
I'll escape another way.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.730
Roger that. Stay safe.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:21:00.150
Take care of the Spirits, Shido Itsuka.
And please, save Zodiac.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.740
Just how many enemies are there?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.370
I don't know, so let's hurry!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.460
That's...!

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.340
Westcott...

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.130
Well, well.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:28.800
I finally tracked down
Elliot and you guys show up.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:34.350
It's lovely to see you again,
but I need you bunch to behave.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.770
I'll play with you after Elliot.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.000
"Episode 04:
'Space Spirit.'"

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:29.800
Once upon a time,
there was a man named Shido Itsuka.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:35.260
Who awaits Shido, Momotaro,
and Little Red Riding Hood at the ball?

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:38.470
Next time: "Fairy Tale."

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:41.540
"Episode 04: 'Fairy Tale.'"

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:41.540
The emperor has no clothes.
